.TH VDR-SUITE-BACKEND-AGENT-ADMIN 8 "August 2026" "VDR-Suite" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
vdr-suite-backend-agent-admin \- inspect or revoke a local VDR-Suite Backend Agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vdr-suite-backend-agent-admin
.RI [ --database " PATH" ]
.RI [ --backend " ID" ]
.RB ( --status |
.B --revoke
.RI [ --reason " TEXT" ])
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vdr-suite-backend-agent-admin
is the local, accountable operational interface for the bounded Phase-63
Backend Agent lifecycle.  It never prints credential or enrollment secrets.
.PP
.B --status
prints one JSON object containing the derived Agent state, generations,
heartbeat/capability revisions and the bounded read-only capability facts.
.PP
.B --revoke
revokes the currently active Agent bound to the selected Backend, including
its device and credential identity.  Revoked history remains persisted so a
replacement enrollment can be distinguished from the old Agent.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --database " PATH"
SQLite database path.  The default is
.IR /var/lib/vdr-suite/vdr-suite.db .
.TP
.BI --backend " ID"
Backend binding.  The default is
.BR default .
.TP
.B --status
Print the current derived Agent state as JSON.
.TP
.B --revoke
Revoke the active Agent for the Backend.
.TP
.BI --reason " TEXT"
Bounded accountability reason used with
.BR --revoke .
The default is
.BR operator-revoked .
.SH SECURITY
Run this utility only from the trusted local administrator context.  Output
contains identifiers and state only; it does not expose enrollment tokens,
credential secrets, verifiers, cookies or process environment.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/vdr-suite/vdr-suite.db
Default Control-Plane database.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vdr-suite-backend-agent (8),
.BR vdr-suite-backend-agent-enroll (8),
.BR vdr-suite-daemon (8)
